acronyms are often positive. Space/punctuation, case, length, consonant
clusters, and the preceding final character distinguish these responses.
Document starts strengthen the negative response. Smaller rules cover Georg-
names, the JavaScript abbreviation js, and a few related g/j letters in other
scripts. All remaining tokens receive a near-zero baseline. This is not a
semantic classifier or a complete account of token-specific effects.
